<article class="env-proposition" id="05K2">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05K2">Proposition <span data-tag="05K2">4.7.9.22</span>.</a> Let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be an $\infty $-category and let $n$ be an integer. Let $X$ be an object of $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$, and let us abuse notation by identifying $X$ with its image in the homotopy $n$-category $\operatorname {h}_{\mathit{\leq {}n}}{\mathit{(\operatorname{\mathcal{C}})}}$ (Notation <a data-tag="0598" href="/tag/0598">4.7.9.2</a>). Then $X$ is $(n-1)$-truncated if and only if the diagram of $\infty $-categories </p>
<div class="equation" id="05K3">
<span class="equation-label"><a data-tag="05K3" href="/tag/05K3">4.79</a></span>
<div>\begin{equation}  \begin{gathered}\label{equation:discrete-via-slicing} \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{/X} \ar [r] \ar [d] &amp;  \operatorname {h}_{\mathit{\leq {}n}}{\mathit{(\operatorname{\mathcal{C}})}}_{/X} \ar [d] \\ \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\ar [r] &amp;  \operatorname {h}_{\mathit{\leq {}n}}{\mathit{(\operatorname{\mathcal{C}})}} } \end{gathered} \end{equation}</div>
</div>
<p> is a categorical pullback square. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      Since the vertical maps in the diagram (<a data-tag="05K3" href="/tag/05K3">4.79</a>) are right fibrations (Proposition <a data-tag="018F" href="/tag/018F">4.3.6.1</a>), it is a categorical pullback square if and only if, for every object $Y \in \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$, the induced map of right-pinched morphism spaces 
    <p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \theta : \operatorname{Hom}_{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}^{\mathrm{R}}( Y,X) = \{ Y\}  \times _{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}} \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{/Y} \rightarrow \{ Y\}  \times _{ \operatorname {h}_{\mathit{\leq {}n}}{\mathit{(\operatorname{\mathcal{C}})}} } (\operatorname {h}_{\mathit{\leq {}n}}{\mathit{(\operatorname{\mathcal{C}})}})_{/X} = \operatorname{Hom}_{\operatorname {h}_{\mathit{\leq {}n}}{\mathit{(\operatorname{\mathcal{C}})}}}^{\mathrm{R}}( Y,X) \]
</div>
<p>
       is a homotopy equivalence (see Corollary <a data-tag="01VE" href="/tag/01VE">5.1.6.4</a>). It follows from Corollary <a data-tag="059E" href="/tag/059E">4.7.9.8</a> that $\theta $ exhibits $\operatorname{Hom}_{\operatorname {h}_{\mathit{\leq {}n}}{\mathit{(()}}\operatorname{\mathcal{C}})}^{\mathrm{R}}( Y,X)$ as an $(n-1)$-truncation of $\operatorname{Hom}_{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}^{\mathrm{R}}( Y,X)$. In particular, it is a homotopy equivalence if and only if $\operatorname{Hom}_{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}^{\mathrm{R}}( Y,X)$ is $(n-1)$-truncated. This condition is satisfied for every object $Y \in \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ if and only if the object $X$ is $(n-1)$-truncated (Remark <a data-tag="05ED" href="/tag/05ED">4.7.1.2</a>). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
